    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so with horizontal scaling, what are the biggest risks or things that can go wrong during that process? like, what's the main thing that causes a system to fail even when we have auto-scaling set up?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The biggest risk with horizontal scaling is complexity, often related to how the added servers communicate with each other, known as state management. If your application requires session data or specific user information to be stored on a single server, adding more servers won't help if they can't share or access that state consistently. Another risk is network overhead as more instances communicate with each other.",
